  "method": [
    "One isolated test-host process; concurrency levels run sequentially, each with a fresh ephemeral URLSession and the matching maximum connections per host.",
    "A task group maintains up to the selected concurrency until 64 requests settle. Every completed response must retain the original Item/window identity and Hotel/Original notes/Todo/Active values.",
    "ContinuousClock records end-to-end URLSession latency. Completed-request percentiles use nearest rank; counts classify completed, rejected, cancelled and failed outcomes separately.",
    "Mach TASK_VM_INFO reads actual process footprint/resident counters. The entire returned structure is required. Kernel process-lifetime peaks are cumulative and do not reset between workloads.",
    "Trial footprint peaks sample baseline and request completions. They may miss transient peaks between samples. Settled memory is observed after URLSession invalidation and a 250 ms pause.",
    "Final public Core reads/query/recovery inspection retain original content, flags, updatedAt, field hashes, one Item, the original acknowledged checkpoint and no prepared proposal."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One local Debug run with one Item and native test-host overhead; no sustained-load, general capacity, leak-free or saturation guarantee.",
